  <p class="mt-6 text-base md:text-lg text-gray-600">Caveats to keep me honest: every curve is a single training run (no error bars), the data is synthetic, and the encoder is deliberately small. BatchNorm runs at PyTorch's <b>default</b> momentum — the checkpoint lottery is reproduced through the <i>data regime</i> (rare scale outliers arriving with variable gaps over a long run), and the smooth-loss opening figure additionally uses gradient accumulation, the small-scale stand-in for the real run's large effective batch. The repository documents all of this. It's a faithful reproduction of the <i>mechanism</i>, not a benchmark.</p>

